files=sorted(BASE.glob('[0-9][0-9]-*.json'))
profiles={json.loads(p.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))['id']:(p,json.loads(p.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))) for p in files}
def get(n): return profiles[n][1]
def add(n,s):
    o=get(n); sid=f's{len(o["sources"])+1}'; o['sources'].append({'id':sid,**s}); return sid
def gap(n,field,reason,url): get(n)['verification_gaps'].append({'field':field,'reason':reason,'next_source':url})

overviews={
1:['Adhiparasakthi Agricultural College is based at G. B. Nagar in Kalavai, Ranipet district. It is affiliated to Tamil Nadu Agricultural University and focuses on agriculture education, research and rural development. Its learning environment combines academic study with laboratory and farm facilities.','The four-year agriculture degree brings crop, soil and plant-health subjects into practical settings. The published course outline includes rural work experience and skill-based activities, giving applicants specific elements to discuss when comparing colleges. Ask how farm assignments and rural learning are scheduled for the intended cohort, alongside the current entry requirements and full residential or day-scholar costs.'],
2:['Adhiyamaan College of Agriculture and Research was established by AERI Trust in 2016. The college describes a 122.5-acre setting at Athimugam, around 22 kilometres from Hosur. Its TNAU affiliation provides the academic framework for the undergraduate agriculture programme.','The degree brings together crop improvement, plant protection, agricultural engineering, economics and extension. ACAR also publishes departmental material that helps applicants look beyond the course title: its plant-protection section describes insect specimens, microscopy and applied insect-related learning resources. A campus visit can examine how those resources support practical classes and how laboratory study connects with crop problems.'],
3:['J.K.K. Munirajah College of Agricultural Science is a TNAU-affiliated agriculture college in the Erode region. Institutional historical material dates its start to 2014, and a dated college invitation identifies its location at T.N. Palayam, Gobi.','The crop-management curriculum connects cultivation decisions with scientific analysis. Published subject areas include agronomy, soil science, microbiology, crop physiology and agricultural engineering. The course table provides concrete examples for prospective students, from practical crop production to rainfed agriculture and soil-fertility management. Applicants can use those topics to discuss their interests and request the current laboratory and fieldwork timetable.'],
4:['JSA College of Agriculture and Technology is based around Ma. Podaiyur and Avatti, near Tholudhur in Cuddalore district. Sri Venkateswara Educational Trust, Salem, established the college in 2015. It is affiliated to TNAU, with agricultural communities surrounding its highway-corridor location.','The college describes learning through projects, fieldwork and rural agricultural experience. Its published support includes computer and language laboratories, while the training and placement cell describes interview and competitive-examination preparation. Applicants considering undergraduate agriculture can ask how classroom learning, field assignments and rural activities are balanced, and confirm which practical modules are available for their cohort.'],
5:['PGP College of Agricultural Sciences was established in 2013 and is affiliated to Tamil Nadu Agricultural University. Its dedicated college website describes a campus near the Kolli Hills and additional field training at the group’s main campus in Paramathi.','The agriculture degree is taught over eight semesters and combines crop science with agricultural economics and practical subjects. Its published curriculum gives examples of seed treatment, sowing, nursery techniques and crop diagnosis. Applicants can explore how those practical elements develop through the programme while comparing the university counselling and management admission channels described by the college.'],
6:['Pushkaram College of Agriculture Sciences was established in 2016 in the Pudukkottai region. Its institutional brochure places it on the Pudukkottai–Pattukottai route via Alangudi, near Thiruvarangulam and the Vamban agricultural research area.','PCAS offers B.Sc. (Hons.) Agriculture under TNAU affiliation. For a prospective student, the rural setting provides the context for a crop-science education; the next useful step is to inspect the current teaching farm, laboratories and practical calendar. Nearby external research institutions should be treated as separate organisations unless a current student-training arrangement is confirmed.'],
7:['The Indian Agriculture College is located on the Kavalkinaru–Radhapuram Road in Tirunelveli district. Established in 2016 under Joshua Educational and Charitable Trust, it focuses on agricultural education and the farming needs of southern Tamil Nadu.','Its four-year degree is organised over eight semesters. The course page covers agricultural science alongside surveying, soils, water management and allied subjects. The college also publishes campus material grouped around laboratories, agricultural fields, farms and industrial visits. Applicants can use those resources to identify which practical areas interest them and request the current timetable for field and laboratory learning.'],
8:['Palar Agricultural College was established in 2017 under RS Educational and Charitable Trust. It is located at Kothamarikuppam Village, Mailpatti Post, in Vellore district and offers a four-year B.Sc. (Hons.) Agriculture under TNAU affiliation.','Its academic divisions cover crop science and associated subjects, with agricultural teaching units and student-support cells listed across the campus website. The extension department describes rural learning and farmer engagement through RAWE. Applicants can ask how the teaching units and village activities fit together across the degree, while confirming admission ranking requirements and the complete cost of attendance.'],
9:['Thanthai Roever Institute of Agriculture and Rural Development belongs to the Roever educational group and is run by St. John Sangam Trust. Its history records agriculture diploma teaching from 1994 and horticulture diploma teaching from 2001, with degree education developed later.','At Valikandapuram, the college describes 51.97 hectares, or 128.4 acres, used for practical learning and a crop cafeteria. Students considering the agriculture degree can ask how crop observations and field assignments connect with laboratory teaching. TRIARD also publishes scholarship-cell support and named graduate destinations, which applicants can discuss alongside a current prospectus and a recent cohort report.'],
10:['Udai Pratap College is an autonomous institution in Varanasi affiliated to Mahatma Gandhi Kashi Vidyapith. Its 2026–27 prospectus lists B.Sc. (Hons.) Agriculture alongside the wider college’s science, commerce and humanities courses. Agriculture is therefore part of a broader college academic setting.','The agriculture-farm section covers crop production and allied activities, including dairy, poultry, fishery and beekeeping. The prospectus also lists postgraduate subjects in agricultural economics, animal husbandry and dairy, soil science and horticulture. Applicants can compare the undergraduate practical experience and later subject options while checking the college’s entrance-examination conditions for their intended entry year.'],
11:['SBVR Agricultural College is part of the institutions promoted by Badvel & Sidhout Higher Education Committee. Established for the 2016–17 period, it is located in Badvel, YSR Kadapa district, and affiliated to Acharya N. G. Ranga Agricultural University.','The college describes departmental laboratories and a separate agricultural farm, with practical work connecting scientific subjects to cultivation. Its material also identifies experiential learning and village-based RAWEP. These give applicants concrete areas to inspect: the crop assignments students undertake, how fieldwork is assessed, and the current training calendar. Admission enquiries should also confirm the applicable Intermediate or diploma route and the sanctioned entry-year seat allocation.'],
12:['N.S. Agricultural College was established by Sri NS Educational Society in 2016. Located at Gobburu, eight kilometres from Markapur according to the college, it is affiliated to Acharya N. G. Ranga Agricultural University.','Its teaching farm is spread across the main campus and Thokapalli, with instructional units spanning crops, horticulture and crop protection. The four-year degree describes final-year rural experience, experiential learning and an agriculture-related internship. That practical structure is useful for students comparing field exposure: request the current unit allocations, village-work schedule and internship supervision arrangements alongside the entry-year admission notice.']}
